-- Washington: Engrossed Second Substitute House Bill 1170, Chapter 167, Laws of 2026.
-- Sections 1 (definitions), 2 (provenance data), 3(2) (business-to-business),
-- 5 (exclusions) and 9 (effective date).
--
-- Source: source/wa-e2shb-1170-session-law-2026.pdf. Quotations are copied from
-- source/text/wa-e2shb-1170-2026.txt.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `labelling-domain`

§ `The judgements section 2 hands to someone`

DECLARE `Washington section 2 judgements` HAS
    -- s.2(4): "'materially altered' means a significant change that substantially
    -- alters the data in content." Asked only of alterations that are not on the
    -- list of minor modifications.
    `the alteration is a significant change that substantially alters the data in content` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s.2(1): "To the extent commercially and technically reasonable"
    `including provenance data is commercially and technically reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Sec. 9 -- effective date`

-- "This act takes effect February 1, 2027."
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Washington act is in effect on` d IF
    d AT LEAST (YMD 2027 2 1)

§ `Sec. 1 -- definitions`

-- s.1(2): "'Covered provider' means a person or entity that creates, codes, or
-- otherwise produces a generative artificial intelligence system that has over
-- 1,000,000 monthly users and is publicly accessible within the geographic
-- boundaries of the state to consumers for personal use. 'Covered provider' does
-- not include state, local, and tribal governments."
@ref E2SHB 1170 (2026), s.1(2)
GIVEN provider IS A `the provider of the AI system`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provider is a covered provider in Washington` provider IF
        provider's `the monthly users of its system` GREATER THAN 1000000
    AND provider's `its system is publicly accessible in Washington to consumers for personal use`
    AND NOT provider's `it is a state, local, or tribal government`

-- s.1(3): "'Generative artificial intelligence' means technology that uses machine
-- learning ... to generate images, audio, or video." Text is outside it, and s.2(1)
-- reaches only "video, image, or audio content, or content that is any combination
-- thereof".
GIVEN content IS A `piece of content`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is video, image, or audio content` content IF
        elem `image` (content's `the kinds it contains`)
    OR  elem `video` (content's `the kinds it contains`)
    OR  elem `audio` (content's `the kinds it contains`)

§ `Sec. 2(4) -- materially altered`

-- "'Materially altered' does not include minor modifications that do not lead to
-- significant changes to the perceived content or meaning of the content. Minor
-- modifications include: Changes to brightness, contrast, or color; sharpening;
-- saturating; applying filters; resizing; scaling; cropping; format conversions;
-- resampling; denoising; and removal of background noise in audio."
-- "include" makes this list OPEN: an alteration on it is never material, and one
-- off it is material only if it is "a significant change that substantially alters
-- the data in content", which is a judgement. Contrast California 22757.1(l), which
-- is closed.
@ref E2SHB 1170 (2026), s.2(4)
GIVEN a IS A `kind of alteration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is on Washington's list of minor modifications` a IF
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `a change to brightness, contrast, or color` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sharpening`                                 THEN TRUE
    WHEN `saturating`                                 THEN TRUE
    WHEN `applying a filter`                          THEN TRUE
    WHEN `resizing`                                   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `scaling`                                    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `cropping`                                   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `file format conversion`                     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `resampling`                                 THEN TRUE
    WHEN `denoising`                                  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `removal of background noise in audio`       THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN content IS A `piece of content`, judged IS A `Washington section 2 judgements`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the content was materially altered` content judged IF
        any (GIVEN a YIELD NOT `it is on Washington's list of minor modifications` a)
            (content's `the alterations an AI system made to it`)
    AND judged's `the alteration is a significant change that substantially alters the data in content`

§ `Sec. 3(2) and Sec. 5 -- what the chapter does not reach`

-- s.3(2): "Nothing in this chapter may be construed to apply to any
-- business-to-business uses, sales, licensing, or distribution of generative
-- artificial intelligence systems."
-- s.5(1): "This chapter does not apply to any product, service, internet website, or
-- application that provides exclusively video game or interactive experiences ..."
-- s.5(2): "This chapter does not apply to systems used solely for upscaling, noise
-- reduction, or compression."
GIVEN provider IS A `the provider of the AI system`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Washington chapter does not reach the provider's system` provider IF
        provider's `the use is business-to-business`
    OR  provider's `its product exclusively provides video games or interactive experiences`
    OR  provider's `its system is used solely for upscaling, noise reduction, or compression`

§ `Sec. 2(1) -- the duty to include provenance data`

-- "To the extent commercially and technically reasonable, a covered provider shall
-- include provenance data in any video, image, or audio content, or content that is
-- any combination thereof, created or materially altered by the covered provider's
-- generative artificial intelligence system and that is subject to the terms of this
-- chapter."
@ref E2SHB 1170 (2026), ss.1, 2(1), 2(4), 3(2), 5, 9
GIVEN content IS A `piece of content`, provider IS A `the provider of the AI system`, judged IS A `Washington section 2 judgements`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` content provider judged d IF
        `the Washington act is in effect on` d
    AND `the provider is a covered provider in Washington` provider
    AND NOT `the Washington chapter does not reach the provider's system` provider
    AND `it is video, image, or audio content` content
    AND (    content's `how it came to exist` EQUALS `generated by an AI system`
         OR  `the content was materially altered` content judged)
    AND judged's `including provenance data is commercially and technically reasonable`

-- s.2(1), second sentence: "The provenance data must allow a user to assess whether
-- image, video, or audio content ... was created or materially altered by the
-- covered provider's generative artificial intelligence system."
-- s.1(4): "'Provenance data' means data that is embedded into digital content or
-- that is included in the digital content's metadata for the purpose of verifying
-- the digital content's authenticity, origin, or history of modification."
-- A C2PA manifest that declares a generative source type is such data, and lets a
-- user make the assessment.
GIVEN content IS A `piece of content`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the content carries provenance data that lets a user assess whether it was created or materially altered by a generative AI system` content MEANS
    CONSIDER content's `the C2PA manifest it carries`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST m  THEN
            elem `trained algorithmic media` (m's `the source types it declares`)
        OR  elem `composite with trained algorithmic media` (m's `the source types it declares`)
        OR  m's `it carries an AI disclosure assertion`

§ `Sec. 2(2) -- difficult to remove, and the C2PA safe harbour`

-- "A covered provider must use commercially and technically reasonable methods to
-- make the provenance data difficult to remove or tamper with. The use of a commonly
-- supported technical standard for watermarking or metadata, such as the coalition
-- for content provenance and authenticity specification, for provenance data is
-- considered compliant with this subsection."
-- This answers only whether the content is DEEMED compliant with s.2(2) by the safe
-- harbour. Content that is not may still comply, by "commercially and technically
-- reasonable methods"; that is not computed.
-- Content with no C2PA manifest but an imperceptible watermark may still be within the
-- safe harbour, if that watermark follows "a commonly supported technical standard for
-- watermarking". This encoding does not hold that fact, so it refuses there.
@ref E2SHB 1170 (2026), s.2(2)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`whether this watermark follows a commonly supported technical standard is not modelled` MEANS
    REFUSE "whether this watermark follows a commonly supported technical standard is not modelled"

@ref E2SHB 1170 (2026), s.2(2)
GIVEN content IS A `piece of content`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`its provenance data is deemed compliant with section 2(2)` content MEANS
    CONSIDER content's `the C2PA manifest it carries`
    WHEN JUST m  THEN TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF   content's `it carries an imperceptible watermark`
        THEN `whether this watermark follows a commonly supported technical standard is not modelled`
        ELSE FALSE
